odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part2-packages.txt:509:•The MIME media type of each file in the package. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part2-packages.txt:523:If a MIME media type for a document exists, then an OpenDocument package should contain a file with name “mimetype”. The content of this file shall be the ASCII encoded MIME media type associated with the document. See [RFC6838].
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part2-packages.txt:963:The manifest:media-type attribute specifies the MIME media type of a file or directory. See [RFC6838].
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part2-packages.txt:965:A manifest:media-type attribute should be present for all files and directories where a MIME media type exists for the content of the file, or the document or sub document contained in a directory.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part2-packages.txt:1013:The interpretation of the attribute value depends on the MIME media type specified in the manifest:media-type attribute.
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part2-packages.txt:1161:The pkg:mimeType property is used to specify the MIME media type [RFC6838] of file described by an pkg:File class or one of its subclasses.
